# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CRM Workspace — environment variable template
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development and fill in the
# values for the phase you are working on. Never commit real environment
# files: `.gitignore` excludes `.env*` (this example file is the only
# tracked exception).
#
# Current status: Phase 3 (workspaces & team) is active. The two Supabase
# values below are required for sign-in/sign-up flows and workspace
# features; the application still builds and runs without them (auth
# screens show a configuration notice). Full setup:
# docs/SUPABASE_SETUP.md.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase (Phase 2: authentication · Phase 3+: database) ───────────
# Public values: safe to reference from browser code.
# Find them in your Supabase project under Settings → API Keys.
# The publishable key is the same value Supabase formerly called "anon".
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── Supabase service role (SERVER-ONLY SECRET) ────────────────────────
# ⚠️ Bypasses Row Level Security. NOT used by the application in Phase 3
# (kept here for later phases). Must only be used in trusted server-side
# code (migrations, webhooks, admin jobs). Never prefix with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_. Never expose to the browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Resend — workspace invitation emails (Phase 3) ────────────────────
# ⚠️ SERVER-ONLY SECRETS. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL must be a plain address on a domain VERIFIED in the
# Resend dashboard (e.g. no-reply@your-domain.com). With either value
# missing, inviting teammates fails with an explicit configuration
# error — the app never pretends an email was sent.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=
